Appendix F — Persistent Excitation: Complete Treatment

F.1 Definitions

Definition F.1 (PE of a regressor sequence). A sequence $\{\Phi_t\}_{t=0}^{N-1} \subset \mathbb{R}^{d \times p}$ is persistently exciting of order $K$ if there exist $c > 0$ and $N_0 \in \mathbb{N}$ such that for all $N \geq N_0$,

\sum_{t=0}^{N-1} \Phi_t \Phi_t^\top \succeq c I_d. \tag{F.1}

Definition F.2 (PE for input sequences). A scalar input sequence $\{u_t\}$ is persistently exciting of order $K$ if the regressor $\Phi_t = [u_t, u_{t-1}, \ldots, u_{t-K+1}]^\top$ satisfies (F.1).

F.2 PE is not sufficient for consistency

Theorem F.1. PE of $\{\Phi_t\}$ is necessary but not sufficient for consistency of the least-squares estimator $\hat{\theta}_N = (\sum_t \Phi_t \Phi_t^\top)^{-1} \sum_t \Phi_t Y_t$.

Proof. PE ensures $\sum_t \Phi_t \Phi_t^\top$ is invertible, so $\hat{\theta}_N$ is well-defined. However,

\hat{\theta}_N - \theta^\star = \left(\sum_t \Phi_t \Phi_t^\top\right)^{-1} \sum_t \Phi_t \epsilon_t. \tag{F.2}

Consistency requires $\sum_t \Phi_t \epsilon_t \to 0$ in probability. This holds under (i) $\mathbb{E}[\epsilon_t | \Phi_t] = 0$ (correct model), (ii) bounded moments, and (iii) ergodicity. PE alone does not imply any of these. $\blacksquare$

F.3 PE and Fisher information

Lemma F.1. Under correct specification, the per-observation Fisher information satisfies

I_1(\theta^\star) = \frac{1}{\sigma^2} \mathbb{E}[\Phi_t \Phi_t^\top], \tag{F.3}

for Gaussian noise with variance $\sigma^2$. Therefore PE is equivalent to positive-definiteness of $I_1$.

F.4 Induced regressors for the diagnostic experiment

For the PCI problem with diagnostic perturbation $\delta U_t = \delta_t v^\star$ and induced regressor

\Phi_t = \mathscr{O}_K^B \, v^\star \delta_t, \tag{F.4}

PE requires

\sum_{t=0}^{N-1} \delta_t^2 \, \mathscr{O}_K^B v^\star (\mathscr{O}_K^B v^\star)^\top \succeq c I. \tag{F.5}

Since $\mathscr{O}_K^B v^\star$ is a fixed vector, this is equivalent to

\sum_{t=0}^{N-1} \delta_t^2 \geq \frac{c}{\|\mathscr{O}_K^B v^\star\|^2}. \tag{F.6}

F.5 Sufficient excitation condition

Proposition F.1. If $\|\mathscr{O}_K^B v^\star\| > 0$ and $\sum_t \delta_t^2 \to \infty$, then the induced regressors are PE.

Proof. Immediate from (F.6). $\blacksquare$

Remark F.1. The condition $\|\mathscr{O}_K^B v^\star\| > 0$ is precisely the channel-separation-plus-dynamic-excitation condition. If $\mathscr{O}_K^B v^\star = 0$, no amount of diagnostic input can excite the relevant directions, and PE fails.

