Appendix L — Consolidated Standing Assumptions

Regularity (R0). Markov kernels $\mathcal{K}_\theta$ and $\mathcal{L}_\phi$ are Borel-measurable, and the joint law exists by Ionescu-Tulcea.

Compactness (C1). $\mathcal{Q}(\mathcal{D}_t, U)$ is compact in a topology making $M \mapsto P_M(T(X_T) \mid U, \mathcal{D}_t)$ continuous.

Moments (C2). $\mathbb{E}_M[|T(X_T)|] < \infty$ for all $M \in \mathcal{Q}$.

Measurable selection (C3). The supremum in $\Gamma_{\mathrm{PC}}$ is attained.

Smoothness (A1). $F_\theta, h_\phi \in C^\infty$ on a compact admissible set $K$.

Correct specification (A1'). $M^\star \in \mathcal{Q}$.

Channel identifiability (A4). There exists a consistent estimator $\widehat{D_U h}_N \to D_U h$ under the diagnostic protocol.

Target observability (A5). $\ker \mathcal{O}_K \subseteq \ker dT$.

Persistent excitation (A6). Induced regressors $\Phi_t$ satisfy (F.1).

Consistent contraction (A7). $\mathcal{Q}_N \to [M^\star]_{\mathcal{D},U}$ in probability.

Uniform continuity (A8). $M \mapsto P_M(T(X_T) \mid U, \mathcal{D}_t)$ is uniformly continuous on $\mathcal{Q}$.

Constant rank (CR). $\mathcal{O}_F(h)$ has constant rank on $K$.

Fisher regularity (H1). $\ell_N$ is $C^2$ in $\vartheta$; $I_1(\vartheta) \succ 0$ uniformly on $\Theta$; $\hat{\vartheta}_N$ exists and is consistent.

Lipschitz target map (H2). $g$ is Lipschitz with constant $L_T < \infty$ in the Fisher metric.

Hölder class (H3). $\Theta \subseteq \mathcal{H}^\beta(\mathcal{X})$ with radius $R$ and entropy bound (H.13).

